      "note": "`:role` is permitted deliberately (#875): the model resolves and validates it against the configured SPARC_AUTH_BOUNDARY_ROLES vocabulary in one place, so the API and UI cannot disagree about what is acceptable. A hand-rolled controller allowlist previously checked the DISPLAY list while the enum enforced its own keys, which 500'd on a valid configured label. Privilege escalation is prevented by AUTHORIZATION, not by the permit list: both the API and (as of the #913/#912 follow-up branch) the web controller gate every write behind `authorization_boundaries.write`. The web path had NO such gate before that fix — see spec/requests/authorization_boundary_memberships_authz_spec.rb, which fails if it is removed.",
