      "fingerprint": "a5232caf38eda922c2ea4b123a4fff9f40b804fc25205cea64a39702f57d46ca",
      "note": "AttestationsController#attestation_params permits :attester_user_id and :role. BRAKE0105 fires on the field NAMES (an *_id foreign key and 'role' are both on Brakeman's dangerous-key list), not on a demonstrated unsafe assignment. Neither key can escalate the CALLER's privileges: the caller is already gated by authorize_attestation_write! (evidence.write, scoped to the evidence's authorization boundary), and neither field grants the caller any access. Both values are constrained by the model, not by this permit list. Attestation#attester_holds_the_attested_role (#947) rejects the record unless the NAMED attester actually holds an attesting role on that evidence's boundary, resolved from the evidence.attest permission via the #919/#707 roster — so a forged attester_user_id/role pair cannot be saved. attester_name/attester_email are deliberately NOT permitted; they are snapshotted from the resolved account (#934 rule), which is what stops a request naming one person while referencing another. SUPERSEDES fingerprint 85a0dc658a70..., whose note claimed role was 'descriptive metadata, NOT an app-level authorization' and cited Attestation::ROLES. #947 made both statements false: the role IS now checked against the roster, and ROLES was deleted in favour of permission-derived eligibility. The fingerprint moved because #947 replaced attester_name/attester_email with attester_user_id in this permit list."
